WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.700
Saving electricity starts with small choices: switching off lights,
using air-conditioning carefully, and avoiding unnecessary power use.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:15.500
The result is hard to see,
so motivation often fades.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:26.700
CommonGrid makes every saving visible. Electricity saved becomes points,
personal progress, and momentum towards a shared university reward.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:37.600
Students can see their impact, the university total,
and exactly how close everyone is to the next milestone.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:47.900
For this NUS prototype, students represent their halls
in an Energy Sprint.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:56.200
The hall that saves the most
earns a stronger reward tier.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:05.200
First place unlocks Gold for the top forty percent.
Second place unlocks Silver for the top thirty percent.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:13.800
Students still need to take part.
A hall result alone does not guarantee a reward.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:23.900
The Journey screen builds a habit.
The calendar highlights every day electricity was saved.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:34.400
Streaks show consistency, while achievements recognise
personal and hall milestones.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:43.100
For this demo, an administrator simulates
verified building data.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:50.900
In a full deployment, the same information
could come from IoT-enabled electricity meters.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:59.500
The administrator records eight kilowatt-hours for Alice.
CommonGrid awards eighty points.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:08.000
The university reaches one thousand points,
and three free laundry cycles are unlocked.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:18.300
Kent Ridge earns Silver. Alice ranks twelfth out of eighty,
inside the top twenty-four.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:28.500
Students outside the cutoff keep their progress,
while the reward goes to those who contributed most.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:38.300
CommonGrid gives students immediate feedback,
a reason to work together, and a clear link to campus electricity use.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:47.300
Small savings become visible progress,
friendly competition, and rewards people can genuinely earn.
